[h2]Fixed: the way into the Spartan Crypt, and chest loot that actually varies[/h2]

[b]Read this first if you have played since 6 August.[/b] The only entrance to the Spartan Crypt was broken, and this update repairs it.

[list]
[*][b]The Warden of the Spartan Crypt answers you again.[/b] Deep in the Athens catacombs he simply did not respond when clicked - no dialog box, nothing - and since he is the [i]only[/i] way down, the crypt below him was unreachable. Two things were wrong. His one travel offer was generated through the single code path in the travel system that had never been confirmed working in game; it now comes from the same proven path every other traveller in the mod uses. And he had been placed on exactly the spot both Spartan Crypt teleports drop you on, so an arriving player materialised inside him; he has moved a few paces, still right beside the same stairs down. His menu is unchanged: one option, descend. Sorry for the dead end - that entrance shipped on evidence rather than on a confirmed walk, and this is the correction.
[/list]

[h2]And two loot fixes[/h2]

[list]
[*][b]Chests can finally drop every weapon class - spear included.[/b] Every chest this mod adds inherited one collapsed weapon list that could only pay axes, maces, swords, bows and staves. Spear was simply missing from it, which made a legendary spear [i]structurally impossible[/i] from any mod chest while two dozen of them sat in the database unreachable. Every mod-owned chest and boss hoard now draws from a full-breadth weapon table at its own rarity tier, so Achilles' Spear, Ares' Wrath, Soulharvest, Peleus' Ashen Spear, Telamon's Boar Skewer, Onuris' Spear and the rest are in play. Nothing was removed and no drop chance was lowered - the guaranteed slot keeps its exact weapon-to-relic split, it just is no longer limited to three classes.
[*][b]The guarded chests stop mirroring each other.[/b] The chests in the Polis Daemonai vault-cage, in the Prison of Souls, used to draw from one collapsed pool, so every playthrough looked the same. Each chest now resolves one of three themes when the area loads - martial, hunter or warden for the plain chests, apex, adept or sovereign for the richer ones - so a cage full of chests reads as a cage full of different chests, and re-rolls on a later run.
[*][b]Relics now match the difficulty you are playing.[/b] The guarded chests and the general-guard hoards could pay an Incarnation relic on Normal and an Essence relic on Legendary. Each difficulty branch now drops its own tier - Essence on Normal, Embodiment on Epic, Incarnation on Legendary - and a build-time audit walks every chest chain so a wrong-tier relic cannot come back. Legendary payouts were preserved exactly.
[/list]

